# Fixed defect 2692, 2026-11-22, lane-crossing, a shape beside it: a record
# of another module holding a `ptr`, handed to `spawn`. Symptom: accepted,
# so two threads held one address C owns. Cause: the walk asking whether a
# type reaches a `ptr` or a `cstr` read the record's fields, which were
# lowered only once the declarations' walk reached its module, after the
# root's `main` (spec § 11: a `ptr`, or a value holding one, never crosses).
use raw

function body(r: raw.Raw) -> i64
    return r.n

function main()
    t = spawn(body, raw.made()).must()  #~ thread_crossing
    print(t.wait())
